  "slug": "decoding-mitochondrial-diverse-eukaryotes-557a",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a bioinformatics toolkit extend benchmarked, self-validating pipelines to isoform, transcriptome, and structural variant analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is benchmarked, reproducible processing of sequencing and variant data, with tool outputs checked against established tools or harmonized callsets. pyTransRate reimplements TransRate in Python for reference-free de novo assembly QC using snap and salmon and reports matching original metrics. GaussF performs alignment-free isoform quantification with GC-stratified k-mer Gaussian CDF self-benchmarking, evaluated against Kallisto and Salmon. IG-28 targets isoform identification from large bulk and single-cell full-length cDNA datasets, while OTTER deconvolutes murine host reads from xenograft RNA-seq and bisulfite-seq workflows. CALMeR conditions long-read MAPQ filtering on transcript context. Verix provides multi-breakpoint diagnostic metrics and consensus harmonization across complex structural variant callsets. What is new relative to single-algorithm papers is the emphasis on internal self-validation and cross-callset harmonization, applied to integrated outputs rather than isolated algorithms.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
